# Story 19: Tool Approval (50s)
# Hook: Every destructive tool call needs your approval. You stay in control.
# Duration: 50s
# Source: story-19-tool-approval.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 9

[00:00.0 --> 00:04.0]
Start rysh -- you land in shell mode.

[00:04.0 --> 00:08.0]
Double-press Escape to enter prompt mode.

[00:08.0 --> 00:18.0]
Ask the AI to write a file. It will propose a file_write tool call -- but first, it needs your approval.

[00:18.0 --> 00:23.0]
The approval dialog shows exactly what tool the AI wants to run and what arguments it will use. No surprises.

[00:23.0 --> 00:27.0]
Type y to approve. The file gets created.

[00:27.0 --> 00:32.0]
The AI confirms the file was created successfully.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
Now ask the AI to show the contents -- read tools are non-destructive, so they run without approval.

[00:40.0 --> 00:45.0]
There it is -- Hello World. Written by AI, approved by you.

[00:45.0 --> 00:50.0]
Every write, delete, and execute needs your say-so. You stay in control.

